    "title": "Traffic pattern changing on Washington Avenue in Sheboygan as milling, paving planned - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Brandon Reid ,\n7 hours ago SHEBOYGAN – Two-way traffic on a stretch of Washington Avenue was to be restored starting Wednesday night, Sept. 24, with one lane of traffic in both directions throughout the project length.\nThe traffic impact on Washington Avenue stretches from South Taylor Drive to South Business Drive.\nCity of Sheboygan said much of the traffic will be in the eastbound lanes with cones designating the centerline between traffic directions.\nRead more: Sheboygan's affordable Gateway Apartments construction still on track to finish this fall\nMilling and paving operations are to occur Thursday and Friday, Sept. 25-26, with pavement marking on Monday, Sept. 29.\nThe project is expected to be completed and traffic control removed by the end of the day Monday, Sept. 29, with the roadway fully open to traffic on Tuesday, Sept. 30.\nThe city noted all work and traffic impacts are weather-dependent and subject to change.\nContact Brandon Reid at breid@gannett.com .\nThis article originally appeared on Sheboygan Press: Traffic pattern changing on Washington Avenue in Sheboygan as milling, paving planned",
